🧾 Service Overview

The GCP Unstructured Data Layer (UDL) platform provides a scalable and secure environment for the end-to-end processing of unstructured data, from ingestion and preparation through to AI-driven processing, knowledge generation, and consumption. The platform aligns with the enterprise unstructured data reference architecture and supports capabilities such as document ingestion, content normalisation, semantic processing, and knowledge persistence.

🎯 Purpose

* Enable AI-driven processing and decision support from unstructured data
* Provide a scalable and standardised platform for ingestion, processing, and retrieval of unstructured content
* Support semantic understanding and knowledge generation using LLMs, embedding models, and graph/vector capabilities
* Enable semantic search and contextual retrieval across unstructured data domains
* Establish a foundation for structured, governed, and reusable enterprise knowledge
* Integrate enterprise AI capabilities to support content transformation, validation, and reasoning
* Support onboarding of multiple unstructured data use cases across business domains


UDL Use Cases

The platform supports a range of unstructured data use cases across business domains. As part of this, the Codify the Bank (CTB) use case leverages the platform to transform unstructured policy and procedure documents into structured, validated, and reusable enterprise knowledge. It enables AI-driven reauthoring, validation, and knowledge graph generation to support improved consistency, traceability, and downstream consumption.


* Support manual ingestion and processing of unstructured policy and procedure documents
* Enable AI-driven reauthoring and validation workflows to standardise and improve document quality
* Provide human-in-the-loop review and approval to ensure accuracy and compliance
* Generate structured knowledge artefacts from approved content using knowledge graph modelling
* Enable semantic understanding and retrieval through vector embedding generation
* Support hybrid knowledge retrieval combining graph-based and vector-based approaches
* Provide access to processed content and knowledge outputs via UI and APIs
* Establish a foundation for scalable onboarding of additional unstructured data use cases


