Phase 2 extends the approved CIB UDL platform foundation to support the Codify the Bank reauthoring and validation capability in a production-aligned environment. The focus of this phase is to enable controlled manual ingestion, document preparation, AI-assisted reauthoring, validation, human review, and persistence of processing outputs and metadata.

This phase does not include knowledge graph generation, Neo4j integration, vector embedding, or knowledge management capabilities. These will be addressed separately as part of Phase 3.

Scope — Phase 2

In scope

* Manual ingestion of policy and procedure documents
* Document preprocessing and conversion into structured markdown
* Chunking to support AI-assisted processing
* AI-assisted reauthoring workflow
* Validation workflow to compare outputs against source documents
* Human-in-the-loop review and approval
* Integration with Group AI platform for LLM-based reauthoring and validation
* Storage of source documents, reauthored outputs, validation results, and operational metadata
* UI/API support for upload, review, approval, and output retrieval

Out of scope

* Neo4j integration
* Knowledge graph generation
* Vector embedding generation
* Hybrid retrieval / KG-RAG
* Knowledge management capability
* Event-driven GPPS / GMS source integration
* Fabric publication of data products
* External downstream consumer integrations

Objectives — Phase 2

* Productionise the core Codify reauthoring and validation workflow
* Replace tactical AI integration patterns with Group AI platform integration
* Enable controlled manual document processing through the CTB Workbench
* Ensure AI-generated outputs are reviewed and approved before use
* Persist source, reauthored, validation, and metadata artefacts for traceability
* Establish a governed foundation for Phase 3 knowledge graph, embedding, and retrieval capabilities

